                                        ],
                                        "examples": []
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "yawning",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "dace7bed-af3a-3581-a367-d9c1f9d36dbb",
                                        "entry_id": "7d0d7072-6cc0-30df-ad31-682dfbc40f2e",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The action of the verb yawn."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e5190067-4061-48b3-915b-426f19a98bee",
                                                "sense_id": "dace7bed-af3a-3581-a367-d9c1f9d36dbb",
                                                "text": "Her vivacity appeared as graceful as it was buoyant; her gay spirit seemed the musical overflowings of youth and happiness; her eye and cheek brightened together; and her sweet glad laugh was as catching as yawning."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "yawning",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "01b05d65-052a-30ad-833e-86f270bf3f53",
                                        "entry_id": "71bee34e-28e8-3636-a83f-c1fedc58b146",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "That yawns or yawn."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "77940573-b929-4b4f-8e9e-8c259342a138",
                                                "sense_id": "01b05d65-052a-30ad-833e-86f270bf3f53",
                                                "text": "yawning commuters"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "68af582b-b2ed-33e8-8b8b-717275e773e4",
                                        "entry_id": "71bee34e-28e8-3636-a83f-c1fedc58b146",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Wide open."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "figuratively"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4ed8b845-f297-469c-a09e-d9ddd992c1e4",
                                                "sense_id": "68af582b-b2ed-33e8-8b8b-717275e773e4",
                                                "text": "a yawning chasm; the shark's yawning jaws"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e251e668-b921-47d7-a64a-a371ade9f84f",
                                                "sense_id": "68af582b-b2ed-33e8-8b8b-717275e773e4",
                                                "text": "That experience really taught me something. That deep down inside, I am broken, and that I'm using work to plaster over some yawning gap within myself."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4e3a4c79-ee98-448a-8c55-c74c55238153",
                                                "sense_id": "68af582b-b2ed-33e8-8b8b-717275e773e4",
                                                "text": "The yawning gap in neuroscientists’ understanding of their topic is in the intermediate scale of the brain’s anatomy. Science has a passable knowledge of how individual nerve cells, known as neurons, work. It also knows which visible lobes and ganglia of the brain do what."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d975f578-4596-4129-8b95-fc0387f5a712",
                                                "sense_id": "68af582b-b2ed-33e8-8b8b-717275e773e4",
                                                "text": "But always and ever there is a yawning chasm below[.]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "999aeb08-0ccf-49f4-b780-04348af19b24",
                        "source_entry_id": "7c9b8b13-e1a9-3408-a47a-98949de3c105",
                        "source_sense_id": "493ad166-1595-3434-994f-c4201792e768",
                        "target_lang_word": "yawn",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "yawn",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "6cf356ef-bdfe-36d2-8187-077b3acc04be",
                                        "entry_id": "76bbe544-b166-3e56-9f0d-b1f6ad0efa2a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To open the mouth widely and take a long, rather deep breath, often because one is tired or bored, and sometimes accompanied by pandiculation."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "intransitive"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a6dfb61f-b14f-48fa-b2ab-6998ed6ab706",
                                                "sense_id": "6cf356ef-bdfe-36d2-8187-077b3acc04be",
                                                "text": "I could see my students yawning, so I knew the lesson was boring them."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e2c30665-5cb4-4d09-8875-070fb77574c7",
                                                "sense_id": "6cf356ef-bdfe-36d2-8187-077b3acc04be",
                                                "text": "[…] I found my self towards Evening, first empty and sickish at my Stomach, and nearer Night mightily enclin’d to yawning and sleepy […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a10b6b65-e248-454d-a516-11eb90cb8e62",
                                                "sense_id": "6cf356ef-bdfe-36d2-8187-077b3acc04be",
                                                "text": "c. 1773, John Trumbull, The Progress of Dulness, Exeter, New Hampshire: Henry Ranlet, 1794, Part 1, p. 19,\nAnd while above he spends his breath,\nThe yawning audience nod beneath."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "f0e35743-ab3d-3897-8766-4375f550f463",
                                        "entry_id": "76bbe544-b166-3e56-9f0d-b1f6ad0efa2a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To say while yawning."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "134a90d5-f18e-40f9-b852-b5cffd5c34d4",
                                                "sense_id": "f0e35743-ab3d-3897-8766-4375f550f463",
                                                "text": "“I haven’t the least idea what I want to do,” he yawned."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e1827b87-1229-47ed-9fae-1f152918e149",
                                                "sense_id": "f0e35743-ab3d-3897-8766-4375f550f463",
                                                "text": "“Oh,” Sutherland yawned, “I’m too old for this.”"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "49fa6ff5-c562-3422-ab2f-2d3c1c3136f5",
                                        "entry_id": "76bbe544-b166-3e56-9f0d-b1f6ad0efa2a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To present a wide opening; gape."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "95eede3d-ad9d-4b95-851e-22041c35ec89",
                                                "sense_id": "49fa6ff5-c562-3422-ab2f-2d3c1c3136f5",
                                                "text": "The canyon yawns as it has done for millions of years, and we stand looking, dumbstruck."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ed584823-c10a-4aad-90fc-c3529bff23c8",
                                                "sense_id": "49fa6ff5-c562-3422-ab2f-2d3c1c3136f5",
                                                "text": "Death yawned before us, and I hit the brakes."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "85f9bf9d-e471-443f-a228-abbb2b8e5452",
                                                "sense_id": "49fa6ff5-c562-3422-ab2f-2d3c1c3136f5",
                                                "text": "’Tis now the very witching time of night,\nWhen churchyards yawn, and hell itself breathes out\nContagion to this world."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "09004a11-7b69-4c84-8000-6d8451c7cefb",
                                                "sense_id": "49fa6ff5-c562-3422-ab2f-2d3c1c3136f5",
                                                "text": "[…] Hell at last\nYawning receavd them whole, and on them clos’d,"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a3399517-07eb-4727-8009-6e86c4d3b791",
                                                "sense_id": "49fa6ff5-c562-3422-ab2f-2d3c1c3136f5",
                                                "text": "If your child has tumbled into one of those open sewers which yawn for the unwary in the streets […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "66676c18-15ca-3a71-9033-67cf3fb7a122",
                                        "entry_id": "76bbe544-b166-3e56-9f0d-b1f6ad0efa2a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To open the mouth, or to gape, through surprise or bewilderment."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "8300c404-1dc7-4a1c-8bb1-19d6197f7b5f",
                                                "sense_id": "66676c18-15ca-3a71-9033-67cf3fb7a122",
                                                "text": "[…] O heavy hour!\nMethinks it should be now a huge eclipse\nOf sun and moon, and that the affrighted globe\nShould yawn at alteration."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0f42e97d-c9ae-4f6e-a461-86a8200bfe1c",
                                                "sense_id": "66676c18-15ca-3a71-9033-67cf3fb7a122",
                                                "text": "[…] Hell being vnder euerie one of their Stages, the Players (if they had owed him a spight) might with a false Trappe doore haue slipt him downe, and there kept him, as a laughing stocke to al their yawning Spectators."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "09850ac1-9b48-39ab-a4bd-5682a4fb8fe4",
                                        "entry_id": "76bbe544-b166-3e56-9f0d-b1f6ad0efa2a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "To be eager; to desire to swallow anything; to express desire by yawning."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "obsolete"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4ddba966-cb7a-4da4-b8d9-59f2a228433d",
                                                "sense_id": "09850ac1-9b48-39ab-a4bd-5682a4fb8fe4",
                                                "text": "to yawn for fat livings"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "370e8f10-2f75-4f4f-aa78-69b1e0bbd58d",
                                                "sense_id": "09850ac1-9b48-39ab-a4bd-5682a4fb8fe4",
                                                "text": "Fly not, as thou wert wont, to his embrace,\nLest, after one long yawning gaze, he swear\nThou art the best good fellow in the world,\nBut he had quite forgotten thee, by Jove!"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            },
                            {
                                "target_word": "yawn",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "96f3118a-937a-339e-9f21-78e5e7e40e60",
                                        "entry_id": "d11a51ed-cbe3-3c84-a587-504f70c53e1a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The action of yawning; opening the mouth widely and taking a long, rather deep breath, often because one is tired or bored."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "9cc354c0-9a1c-4e33-849b-74b9bb86a796",
                                                "sense_id": "96f3118a-937a-339e-9f21-78e5e7e40e60",
                                                "text": "At length, quite exhausted by the attempt to be amused with her own book, which she had only chosen because it was the second volume of his, she gave a great yawn and said, “How pleasant it is to spend an evening in this way! […]”"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "04fbc41e-7561-4601-b783-237e61f2c83a",
                                                "sense_id": "96f3118a-937a-339e-9f21-78e5e7e40e60",
                                                "text": "But Mrs. MacWhirr, in the drawing-room […], stifled a yawn—perhaps out of self-respect—for she was alone."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "24614793-58a8-3e80-93b3-7bef2a10ae94",
                                        "entry_id": "d11a51ed-cbe3-3c84-a587-504f70c53e1a",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A particularly boring event."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "colloquial"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b5cec10c-5789-432a-8cf1-4fa203cdfe27",
                                                "sense_id": "24614793-58a8-3e80-93b3-7bef2a10ae94",
                                                "text": "The slideshow we sat through was such a yawn. I was glad when it finished."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
